From a448388bc5696ad0db86159a3f72d5ae203b8e8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:55:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] History sources review: quote the author, not the notes;
 bound omissions (U07)

- An excerpt is matched against the author's text unless its card says it
  quotes a note ("inNote": true). Before, "The blood of Christians is the
  seed of the Church." passed as Tertullian's Apology because a bracketed
  editor's note gives it; the text itself says "the blood of Christians is
  seed". Pliny's letter, in McGiffert's note to Eusebius 3.33, now carries
  inNote.
- Each piece of an excerpt with omissions must begin within 2,000
  characters of the one before, and every occurrence of a piece is tried.
  Before, "the Christian emperors ... are to be worshipped" passed against
  City of God 5 from pieces 112,000 characters apart.
- .prettierignore keeps `pnpm format` off the stored texts, whose sha256 the
  gate checks, and off the generated provenance list.
- PROVENANCE.md states both rules and that editors' headings and summaries
  sit in the author's text; SURVEY.md corrects the Loeb Julian dates and no
  longer says every printed work is long out of copyright.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JuCQ8kZ25i9zRwNgk6bh4e
